    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** standing as our clear premier asset. With an elite efficiency score of 81.85, **Corbin Carroll** capitalizes on a favorable matchup against King, M, where the combination of a high-ceiling leadoff spot and a moderate SB suppression threat from the pitcher profile creates an optimal environment for production. **Brice Turang** follows closely at 75.05; his value is bolstered significantly by his leadoff position and a targetable matchup against Chandler, whose delivery cadence offers a distinct edge for **Brice Turang** to secure the steals that are paramount to our league strategy. \n\nStrategic lineup construction today heavily weights platoon advantages and situational geometry. While **Mickey Moniak** carries a respectable 49.97 score, he remains our most marginal start, constrained by a negative platoon split against Seymour. His selection is driven largely by park factors, but he sits on the razor's edge; had we healthy depth, he would be the first to yield. Conversely, **Isaac Paredes** (68.21) and **Gabriel Moreno** (66.10) benefit from high-leverage lineup slots, with **Isaac Paredes** specifically exploiting a vulnerable arm in Bieber, whose high xERA dictates an aggressive start despite neutral park conditions. We continue to monitor the status of **Seiya Suzuki**, whose 67.03 score is contingent on confirmed placement in the #2 hole; should he drop down the order, his utility diminishes rapidly.\n\nThe bench remains stagnant due to lingering health concerns, with **Trevor Story** and **Giancarlo Stanton** providing zero contribution while occupying IL slots, and **Josh Naylor** and **Austin Riley** sidelined by scheduled off-days. Depth pieces such as **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Max Muncy** are currently seeing limited volume, while our focus on long-term prospects like **Dalton Rushing**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte** remains strictly custodial. We are currently navigating a thin bench rotation, necessitating that our starters\u2014particularly **James Wood** (63.37)\u2014produce near their efficiency ceilings to offset the lack of replacement-level upside from the reserves.",
